# Front end (public/)

Plain ES modules, one `index.html`, one `css/app.css`. No framework, bundler or npm packages in the browser.

## Patterns

- API: `const data = await api("things", body)` from `core.js` calls `/api/things` (POST with a body, GET
  without), adds the token and throws `Error(message)` on failure. Show failures with `toast(error.message, 3000)` or inline, never `alert()`.
- Rendering: build HTML strings and set `innerHTML`; every dynamic value goes through `esc()`.
- Events: one delegated listener per module on a container (or `document`) using `data-*` attributes:
  `if (e.target.closest("[data-mgr-act]")) ...`. Do not attach listeners per rendered element.
- State: module-level objects; persisted UI choices via `store.get/set` (localStorage `manager.*`).
- Icons: `icon("name")` / `ICONS.spin` from `core.js`; names are the keys of `PATHS` there.
- Dialogs: `<dialog>` in `index.html` with `.help-head` header, a body element and `.fv-foot` footer; open with
  `showModal()`. Add the new ids to the element list in `test/server.test.ts`.
- New section: `view-<name>` in `index.html`, `SECTIONS` in `core.js`, `TITLES` and `showSection()` in `app.js`,
  a wiki article in `wiki.js`.

## Shared code

`public/js/devices.js` is also imported by the server: no DOM, no Node APIs, plain data and functions.

## CSS

- Use the variables in `:root` (`--mustard`, `--panel-2`, `--muted`, `--ok`, `--bad`, ...), never raw colours.
- Reuse existing classes (`.btn`, `.btn.primary`, `.set-row`, `.set-chip`, `.switch`, `.muted-note`) before
  adding new ones; prefix new feature classes (`.wiz-*`, `.mgr-*`).
- Modal dialogs that should hug their content need `height: fit-content`.
- Check phone widths: the browser test fails on sideways scrolling.

## Text

Write for non-technical users: short sentences, name the button they press, say what happens on the handheld.
